# Ordinary text is normalized across platforms. More specific rules below win.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Canonical records are raw Git blobs. Repository filters, keyword expansion,
# working-tree encodings, and semantic merge drivers may not transform them. A
# local .git/info/attributes still outranks this file; this is a repository
# contract, not an enforcement mechanism.
#
# records/ is `-text` rather than the scaffold's `text eol=lf` because it holds
# content-addressed blobs whose filename is their own digest, and end-of-line
# normalization is a byte rewrite. A sibling Frontier already stores a gzip
# stream under records/ that normalization would strip CR pairs out of, so the
# file would no longer hash to its own name. Nothing here is binary yet.
.vela/** -filter -ident -working-tree-encoding -merge -text
records/** -filter -ident -working-tree-encoding -merge -text
artifacts/** -filter -ident -working-tree-encoding -merge -text
frontier.toml -filter -ident -working-tree-encoding -merge diff text eol=lf
